        "description": "An yrast, $J^π=5^-$, spin-trap isomer has been previously identified in $^{32}$Si. The isomeric state decays predominantly via a hindered $E3$ transition [B($E3$) = 0.0841(10)~W.u.], bypassing a nearby $E2$ decay path to the first excited $3^-$ level. The single-neutron aspects of these negative par",
