        "description": "X-ray spectral variability in active galactic nuclei (AGNs) can be either intrinsic or caused by external processes, such as variable absorption. Several transient occultation events from individual clouds or X-ray eclipses have been identified in a number of AGNs in the past two decades. We report ",
